  <story>
    <asA>developer</asA>
    <iWant>changes to any node to automatically flag downstream nodes for review based on graph traversal</iWant>
    <soThat>upstream changes (e.g., requirement revision) visibly ripple to all affected artifacts, making the impact of every change explicit</soThat>
    <tasks>
      <task id="1" ac="1,2">Create impact propagation module
        <subtask>Create lib/impact-propagation.mjs at /home/ubuntu/scripts/lib/impact-propagation.mjs</subtask>
        <subtask>Accept updatedNodeId and projectId as inputs</subtask>
        <subtask>Connect to Memgraph and execute impact traversal query (all edge types, 1-4 hops, active downstream nodes only)</subtask>
        <subtask>Calculate impact score: edge_weight / (hops ^ 1.5) where edge_weight is the weight of the first edge in the path</subtask>
        <subtask>When multiple paths reach the same downstream node, use the highest impact score</subtask>
      </task>
      <task id="2" ac="3,4,5">Implement flagging logic
        <subtask>Score >= 0.5: set status: flagged, flagSeverity: critical, flagReason referencing upstream node</subtask>
        <subtask>Score >= 0.1 and less than 0.5: set status: flagged, flagSeverity: moderate</subtask>
        <subtask>Score less than 0.1: no flag</subtask>
        <subtask>Update flagged nodes in Memgraph via Cypher SET operations</subtask>
        <subtask>Update flagged articles' frontmatter on disk with status: flagged, flagSeverity, flagReason</subtask>
      </task>
      <task id="3" ac="6">Implement impact logging
        <subtask>Append impact record to knowledge/log.md: [IMPACT] {date} | Source: {nodeId} | Critical: N | Moderate: M | Total: T</subtask>
        <subtask>For critical flags, append details about which nodes were flagged</subtask>
        <subtask>Return impact summary as JSON for pipeline event reporting</subtask>
      </task>
      <task id="4" ac="7">Integrate with story compilation
        <subtask>After Knowledge Compiler updates articles, identify nodes with content hash changes</subtask>
        <subtask>For each changed node, call propagateImpact(nodeId, projectId)</subtask>
        <subtask>Impact propagation runs AFTER compilation but BEFORE graph-sync</subtask>
      </task>
      <task id="5" ac="7">Integrate with epic compilation
        <subtask>After epic COMPILER updates maturity scores and marks supersessions, propagate impact for all changed nodes</subtask>
        <subtask>Supersession marking triggers impact propagation on the superseding (new) node, not the superseded (old) node</subtask>
      </task>
      <task id="6" ac="7">Integrate with deployment compilation
        <subtask>After deploy-nodes agent marks code as deployed, propagate impact for status changes</subtask>
        <subtask>Deployment-related impact is lower severity — status changes to deployed are informational</subtask>
      </task>
      <task id="7" ac="7">Integrate with pre-dev compilation
        <subtask>Most critical integration: planning document changes after development flag all downstream code articles</subtask>
        <subtask>Use architecture doc Cypher for requirement-change impact traversal</subtask>
        <subtask>Note: pre-dev compilation is implemented in Epic 4, but engine must support it</subtask>
      </task>
      <task id="8" ac="2">Edge weight configuration
        <subtask>Define edge weights as a configuration object: DEPENDS_ON 1.0, CONFLICTS_WITH 0.9, SUPERSEDES 0.8, DERIVED_FROM 0.7, VALIDATES 0.6, REFINES 0.5, ENABLES 0.5, INFORMS 0.3</subtask>
        <subtask>Impact score formula: EDGE_WEIGHTS[edgeType] / (hops ^ 1.5)</subtask>
        <subtask>Export weights configuration for external adjustment</subtask>
      </task>
    </tasks>
  </story>

  <acceptanceCriteria>
